# Game logic rules

- **All new attacks require a bound/counter.** Document warning, counterplay, cap, scarcity or
  recovery in config and `docs/context/ITEMS.md`.
- **All items must be distinct.** No two items may feel like the same move with different
  numbers. Keep items simple, readable, single-use.
- Power-up rarity uses rank plus score gap (Mario Kart style): trailing players get stronger
  comeback odds without predictable sandbagging. Probability tables must sum to 1.
- Keep game mechanics easy to understand — if a mechanic needs a paragraph to explain in
  the UI, simplify it.
- Scores never go below `SCORING.MIN_SCORE` (0). Use `applyDelta`/`clampScore`.
- Steals and attacks target unbanked (`roundLoot`) or unprotected (Final Plunder) points,
  never a player's whole score.
- Every score change must emit a `RevealEvent` — the reveal queue is the only way players
  learn what happened.
- Mutiny choices, allocations and private item effects use the private state channel.
- Round resolvers in `shared/src/game/` stay pure: inputs in, `{events, deltas, chests}` out.
- Add or update Vitest tests in `shared/src/game/__tests__/` for any scoring/item change.
